<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's June base metals import prices up.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's June base metals import prices up.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's non-ferrous metals import prices rose in June from the previous month due to gains on the London Metal Exchange (LME), the Association of Foreign Trading Agents of Korea (AFTAK) said on Friday.</p>
<p>Import prices of base metals were as follows:</p>
<p>(US$ per tonne on CIF)</p>
<p> METAL		     Origin	Jun     May</p>
<p> Copper (99.95 pct)    Chile     2,696     2,574</p>
<p> Copper scrap (berry)  U.S.	2,513     2,491</p>
<p> Aluminium (99.7 pct)  Australia 1,669     1,723</p>
<p> Lead (99.99 pct)	China	 685	 688</p>
<p> Zinc (99.995 pct)     S.America 1,438     1,408</p>
<p> Nickel (99.9 pct)     Canada    7,355     7,768</p>
<p> Tin (99.85 pct)	 Malaysia  5,645     5,829</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
